# F94 body control (INTENT 11.214) - Titan = 604, a member of the SAME chain
# whose literal was never misspelled.  It fires on BOTH binaries: that is what
# makes the two zeros next to it attributable to the two typos and not to a
# selection that never happened or a table that never runs.
# Observable: the clock, read back through the shipped `get status position`
# (field 4 = JDay).  2035-01-01 = the branch fired, 2036-01-01 = the else fired,
# 2030-01-01 = neither (the play never reached the test).
timerate rate 0
date utc 2030-01-01T00:00:00
select planet Titan
wait duration 1
struct if body_selected equal 604
date utc 2035-01-01T00:00:00
struct if else
date utc 2036-01-01T00:00:00
struct if end
